+# Anti-zombie constraint ties phenomenology to the thick-present tuple
+
+“Zombie” objections lose operational force once experience is identified with the tuple \((G^*, U, B, A, \tau)\) in the thick present. Two systems that match on broadcast clarity \(B\), reflexive access \(A\), urgency/valence \(U\), temporal span \(\tau\), and the self-gradient \(G^*\) cannot drift apart in felt experience without also diverging in adaptation—because the same tagged gradient drives their plasticity and future reports. The residual “ineffable” component is just the Gödel pressure term \(G_t\): a structured model mismatch, not a metaphysical extra fact. Any putative “phenomenon-less twin” that shares the tuple would exhibit the same learning traces; if it behaves differently, the tuple was not actually matched. This is the empirical anti-zombie guarantee recorded in AI_13 lines 16572‑16576 and 16640‑16669.
+
+
+
+
