+# Conscious access can be operationalized by a thick-present coupling scalar
+
+The “minimal, testable consciousness sketch” in AI_13 lines 16793‑16830 defines concrete knobs—urgency \(U_t\), broadcast clarity \(B_t\), reflexive access \(A_t\), thick-present dwell \(\tau\)—and proposes an operational scalar
+\[
+\mathcal{C}_t = I(b_t;\text{Modules}) \times I(b_t;m_t) \times \text{dwell}(b_t) \times \mathrm{Var}(b_t)
+\]
+that detects when the broadcast globally couples modules, includes the self in the loop, sustains availability, and lets valence steer updates. Conscious episodes correspond to regimes where \(\mathcal{C}_t\) exceeds thresholds. This yields falsifiable predictions: varying \(\tau\), clamping \(U_t\), or ablating \(A_t\) should co-vary phenomenology and adaptation; collapse occurs when the scalar falls below dwell/integration bounds.
