+# Change monism removes substance dualism but not the need for invariants
+
+AI_13 explains (lines 17680‑17718) that CO has no physics-vs-qualia dualism: being = changing; selves are metastable invariants of self-modulating flows; indexicals are part of the physical description. This kills the false “stuff A + stuff B” framing and the assumption that we can permute internal codes while holding everything else fixed. Yet reframing alone doesn’t explain why this flow feels this way—you still need indexical anchoring, rigidity proofs, and explicit invariants/predictions. CO must do for consciousness what fluid equations do for vortices: pick out the pattern uniquely and predict its behavior.
+
