+# Change-ontology worldview yields testable commitments and falsifiers
+
+Given CO-0 plus the No-Brute-Boundary norm, AI_13 spells out how the world must look if Change Ontology is right: every change is seeded by prior change; continuity lives at the substrate while discreteness reflects coarse cuts; attractors (negative Lyapunov directions) supply stability and define “identities”; new layers (chemistry, biology, mind) are coordinate compressions on the same flow; and “Gödel pressure” marks where models invent variables. The program advertises concrete bets: damp affect should slow error-weighted learning, hole-density metrics (compression/MDL deficits or Fisher-curvature) should predict where new behaviors/layers arise, and attractor strength should forecast persistence of organisms or neural ensembles. Falsifiers include law-resistant brute events with no precursors, a perfectly predictable fine-grained atlas (no hole regions), or empirical failure of the hole-density and attractor forecasts. Declaring these commitments keeps the ontology auditable rather than rhetorical.
+
+
+
