+# Audit drafts for classical leaks using gauge tests and many-valued logic near Gödel regions
+
+AI_13’s “classical leak” checklist says: treat topology/continuation as primitive, bring in metrics only as gauges; explicitly carry the lens parameter \(\theta\) and judge claims by robustness to small gauge changes; and when working near high Gödel-hole density, allow many-valued/modal statements (“currently undecidable”) rather than force bivalent conclusions. Run gauge tests (re-encode inputs, recompute outputs, track \(R_{\text{lens}}\)), and mark any section that assumes one timeless description or global frame as suspect. The audit keeps Change Ontology from sliding back into classical defaults while signalling where Gödel-driven undecidability legitimately appears.
+
