+# Gödel pressure equals minimal closure failure of a model class on data
+
+AI_13 works out the algebra: Gödel pressure \(\Gamma\) is the minimal closure failure of a model class \(\mathcal{M}\) on data \(D\) (e.g., an observed deficit \(\Delta = L_{\min} - L_T\) between the best achievable compressed length and what a bounded solver attains). Hole density is how often \(\Gamma > \tau\); Gödel holes correspond to dimension births where adding a new variable restores closure. This package (P5–P6) answers “what makes a hole operational?” and nails the definitions needed for experiments and simulations.
+
+
