+# Gödel gaps mark novelty frontiers and boost probe policies
+
+AI_13’s later section emphasizes that Gödel gaps are exactly where new skills/layers are minted. Tasks that treat unknowns as structured gaps—using hedge/probe/jump policies—see a >2× uplift versus ignoring them. Subjects with higher probe-policy scores generate more distinct strategies in creative gaps. The calculus describes identities as attractors, attention as path-weighting, and incompleteness as the signal to switch policies. This note ties the novelty-frontier framing directly to the empirical uplift claims.
+
