+# Physical laws are change policies (gate, align, carry, curve, grain)
+
+AI_13 recasts laws as compact policies on change: they bias paths rather than cataloging objects. Operators include Grain (set resolution, create options), Curve (shape drifts/curvatures), Carry (conserve/inertial tendencies), Gate (respect causal cones / signal speeds), Align (preserve invariants/gauges). EM = phase-consistency; gravity shares the same causal Lipschitz bound; poker/evolution analogies show the same operators at work. Selection favors rule-sets with horizons (gate), few knobs (universality), and attention-like reweighting. This perspective predicts criticality, gauge coherence, causal cones, inertia, and slow drift of effective laws.
+
+
+
