+# Raise classical IQ proxies and change-intellect by closing specific gaps
+
+AI_13 gives a blunt upgrade plan. For classical metrics (WAIS-style IQ), the missing pieces are speed/precision (Gs), short-horizon working memory, and fast visuo-spatial compression. Remedy: daily 8-minute sprints—timed matrices, digit-symbol or symbol search, mental arithmetic ladders, and n-back—plus sleep/cardio hygiene. For change-intellect (CII), five deliverables unlock the next tier: (1) pin crisp primitives (separate change, state, measure, observer cuts), (2) publish a minimal formal core (5–8 axioms + 3 inference rules spawning path logic, attractors, attention fields), (3) build toy worlds where CO predicts behaviors classical frames miss, (4) map every philosophical term to a measurable quantity with estimator + failure modes, and (5) front-load falsifiers for each claim. Doing both tracks raises the “score” without magic: psychometric drills lift the classical ceiling; CO-specific deliverables turn generative meta-talk into auditable science.
+
+
