+sources:
+  - path: TheoryOfChange/00_Meta/AI_RecursiveChats/AI_21.md:169-184
+links_core: []
+---
+# Hypothesis — Zero, infinity, and sign in CO
+
+Claim (speculative)
+- Zero, infinity, and negative values can be read as process states: zero as neutral/identity under a chosen operation, infinity as unbounded loops/divergence beyond tolerance, negative as inverse orientation or debt of bend. Seek CO-consistent interpretations that avoid ad hoc restatement.
+
+Exploratory sketch
+- Map common series/pathological sums (e.g., −1/12 anecdotes) into CO terms: what bend/closure or tolerance regime would give such “results”? Identify where CO must refuse such manipulations vs. where they signal regime change or re-summation.
+
+Questions/falsifiers
+- Does the CO reading add anything beyond existing summation/renormalization theory? Can it specify when a “negative” or “infinite” output is meaningful vs. an artifact of broken assumptions?
*** End Patch
