 # Recursive Truth Value (RTV)
 ## Claim (formal)
 RTV evaluates a claim’s stability across recursive breath cycles under evolving conditions; truth is a fixed point or stable orbit in the validation dynamics.
 
 ## Philosophical Translation (of formal claim)
 Under change, we do not test once — we breathe the test. Truth is what keeps validating as the system and its resolution adjust.
 
+## Philosophical Justification
+In a non‑cessating Δ background, single‑shot truth tests are insufficient; perturbations and resolution shifts alter outcomes. RTV frames validation as an iterated operator over breath cycles (Δ plus observation), treating truth as a fixed point/limit cycle that remains within declared tolerances.
+
 ## Clarifications / Further Context
 - RTV depends on ε, σ(ε), and collapse ⊘ predicates; it complements classical truth with dynamical evaluation.
 
+## Derivation (Philosophical)
+- From [[01_Statements/FoundationalTruth/S-FT-continuity-noncessation]]: validation must accommodate ongoing Δ; recursive evaluation captures stability under change.
+
