 ## Statement (corollary)
 Given Δ(Now), Reach, and Locality, the “prior” is not a static parameter but a recursively updated trace over LocalReach neighborhoods, maintained by pointers and path structure. Hence, prior belief/state evolves with the ongoing change it summarizes.
 
 ## Philosophical Translation
 What you already “have” is not fixed; the very act of continuing updates what counts as your prior.
+
+## Philosophical Justification
+From [[01_Statements/Definition/S-DF-pointer-structural]] and [[01_Statements/Definition/S-DF-reach-relation]], the present structurally refers to reachable elsewhere. Locality and paths ([[01_Statements/Definition/S-DF-locality-prior]], [[01_Statements/Definition/S-DF-path-eventlet-chain]]) restrict and compose that elsewhere, so any “prior” must update with ongoing Δ and reach composition. This ties prior to change rather than a fixed parameter.
*** End Patch
