 ## Statement (corollary)
 Given self‑containment limits, agents must provide explicit “unknown/abstain” modes and defer upward when needed; forced closure induces brittleness.
 
 ## Philosophical Translation
 Honesty about not‑knowing is a feature, not a bug.
+
+## Philosophical Justification
+From incompleteness ([[01_Statements/Definition/S-DF-godel-limits-self-containment]]) and GH markers ([[01_Statements/Definition/S-DF-godel-hole-pointer]]), robust systems must surface abstentions instead of papering over gaps. This design choice follows logically from the impossibility of full self-containment.
@@
