+## Philosophical Translation (of formal claim)
+Consciousness feels intense at the edges of what we can model because that is where the loop does its hardest work: adapting to gaps it cannot pre-close.
+
+## Philosophical Justification
+Given open change and limited models, agents encounter GH where prediction/closure fail. Survival demands meta‑work (resource gating, representation updates) concentrated at those boundaries. The consciousness loop ([[01_Statements/Clarification/S-CL-predictive-loop-control-profile]]) is the mechanism performing that work; hence GH structure selects for such loops.
+
+## Clarifications / Further Context
+- GH are lenses on boundary conditions, not alternative ontologies.
