 ## Claim (formal)
 Locality constrains admissible Reach paths to LocalReach neighborhoods; “prior” denotes reachable positions relative to Now under locality, tracked via field and local pointers.
 
 ## Philosophical Translation (of formal claim)
 Not everything is equally “elsewhere.” What counts as prior is shaped by how change can actually move here and now.
 
+## Philosophical Justification
+Reach ([[01_Statements/Definition/S-DF-reach-relation]]) supplies composability; pointers ([[01_Statements/Definition/S-DF-pointer-structural]]) mark minimal elsewhere. LocalReach bounds what is reachable from Now; “prior” must therefore be defined relative to those bounds, distinguishing field (global) vs local (subject-centered) pointers so that inference and validation respect actual reachability rather than assumed timelines.
+
 ## Clarifications / Further Context
 - Field vs local pointers let us distinguish global vs subject‑centric locality.
+- Locality also constrains evidence aggregation and depth metrics downstream.
 
