 # Action selection / decision dynamics
 ## Claim (formal)
 Decisions are chosen by descending evaluation surfaces under breath‑modulated attention, constrained by invariants and identity preservation.
 
 ## Philosophical Translation (of formal claim)
 We act by following what keeps working as checks continue.
 
+## Philosophical Justification
+- [[S-DF-attention-focus]] picks what to evaluate; [[S-DF-evaluation-surface]] provides a cost landscape.
+- The actor ([[S-DF-actor]]) must choose within RTV/SE budgets; descent methods bound by breath prevent brittle jumps.
+- Identity constraints (from invariants) prune options that would dissolve the subject; therefore action = constrained descent.
+
+## Explanation (informal)
+Action is not a free leap; it is a guided slide down what looks most promising while staying coherent. Focus narrows options, evaluation surfaces grade them, and the actor executes steps that keep SE non‑negative.
+
+## Derivation (Philosophical)
+- Limited attention ⇒ a ranked shortlist.
+- Ranked shortlist + evaluation algebra ⇒ choose steepest viable descent.
+- Choice written to memory traces ⇒ policy update for next cycle.
+
+## Derivation (Formal/Logical/Mathematical)
+```text
+Given Eval: X → L and Attention weighting w,
+Action := argmin_{x∈LocalReach} w(x) ⊗ Eval(x)
+subject to SE(x) ≥ 0 and identity invariants satisfied.
+```
+
+## Proofs/Corollaries References
+- corollary: [[S-CR-action-influences-expectation]]
+- corollary: [[S-CR-recursive-expectation]]
+
+## Clarifications / Further Context
+- “Breath-modulated” means step size and exploration/exploitation ratio adapt to current SE/ε budgets.
+- Failures feed back into evaluation surface via memory traces.
+
+## Next Steps in Chain
+- suggest: [[S-CR-action-influences-expectation]]
+- suggest: [[S-CR-recursive-expectation]]
 
