+# Memory trace and integration — reactivatable tension over experiences
+## Claim (formal)
+A memory trace is a stored structural tension (difference) that can be reactivated across multiple experiences to integrate evidence over time; maintained via attention scheduling and depth‑aware temporal ops.
+
+## Philosophical Translation (of formal claim)
+You can hold a difference so that it can matter later — bringing it back to guide how new moments fit with what you’ve learned.
+
+## Philosophical Justification
+- [[S-DF-reach-relation]] and [[S-DF-locality-prior]] define where traces can anchor; traces compress local differences into reusable pointers.
+- [[S-DF-attention-focus]] and [[S-DF-prm-temporal-ops]] maintain traces without flooding SE; decay by depth prevents stale dominance.
+- Memory as reactivatable tension enables integration across breath cycles while preserving identity constraints.
+
+## Clarifications / Further Context
+- Interacts with LocalReach depth (older traces discounted by depth and EMA).
+- Supports self‑model updates, SE estimation, and expectation formation.
+- Memory encodes patterns of transformation (motion of thought), not static data; integrates as reactivatable tension across cycles.
+
+## Next Steps in Chain
+- suggest: [[S-CR-reactivation-of-tension]]
+- suggest: feed traces into SE/SRL estimation in validation loops.
+
+## Tags
+#type/DF #layer/foundations #domain/recursion #concept/recursive-truth #concept/prior-pointer-reach #status/stable
