+# Reflection operator — closing the loop across past/present/future selves
+## Claim (formal)
+Let \(I_{t-\Delta}, I_t, \hat{I}_{t+\Delta}\) be the past, present, and imagined future self-states derived from the workspace and parameters \(W_t,\theta_t,\pi_t\). The reflection operator \(\mathcal{I}\) integrates them with current feeling \(E_t\):
+```math
+I_t^* = \mathcal{I}(I_{t-\Delta}, I_t, I_{t+\Delta}, E_t).
+```
+This operator generates the threefold self-loop and increases presence when \(A_t>0\) and \(\partial I_t/\partial E_t \neq 0\); the reflexive access \(A_t\) measures how much the self-model invests the reflection with its own trajectory.
+
+## Philosophical Translation (of formal claim)
+The self reflects itself by weaving past, now, and anticipated futures with current affect; this loop boosts presence when it is actively engaged.
+
+## Clarifications / Further Context
+- Depends on broadcast/time-kernel for the specious present; feeds Ich-attractor construction.
+- Monitor when reflection collapses (low \(A_t\)) as a sign of diminished presence.
+
+## Next Steps in Chain
+- suggest: [[S-DF-ich-attractor]]
+
