+# Entropy vs Stabilization Energy
+## Claim (formal)
+High Σ with low SE indicates fragile diversity (novelty/instability); high Σ with high SE indicates robust creativity; low Σ with high SE indicates rigid stability.
+
+## Philosophical Translation (of formal claim)
+How many different ways back matters, but so does how reliably they hold.
+
+## Derivation (Philosophical)
+- Consider Σ as option diversity and SE as persistence budget.
+- Classify regimes: (Σ high, SE low) = brittle spread; (Σ high, SE high) = resilient variety; (Σ low, SE high) = rigidity; (Σ low, SE low) = stagnation/collapse.
+- Map these regimes to intervention policies (increase SE, prune Σ, or encourage exploration).
+
+## Clarifications / Further Context
+- Thresholds are domain/task dependent; declare them when applying.
+- Links to fitness scoring and collapse thresholds.
+
