 # Core CO axiom (CO-0) forbids global stasis without forcing continuity
 
-AI_13 proposes CO-0: change is happening now and never globally stops (no open interval of total stasis). From CO-0 plus a “no-min Δ” premise you obtain scale-freeness but not full continuity; to force continuity you still need a bounded-change-rate or No-Leap axiom. The text distinguishes ontological truths (change-first flow, Gödel pressure as residual diagnostics), modeling stances (metastable patterns, predictive-control view of consciousness), and empirical hypotheses (operator drift predicts resilience, subjective intensity tracks update gradients). Final recommendations: make observability relational, track latent variation budgets, design consciousness assays (stakes → urgency/attention/physiology), run cross-subject alignment pilots, and tidy terminology. This settles what follows logically versus what remains a modeling commitment.
+## Statement (clarification)
+CO‑0 asserts ongoing change: no open interval of total stasis. On its own CO‑0 implies scale‑free change but not continuity; continuity requires an extra “no leap/bounded rate” premise. The clarification separates what is entailed by CO‑0 from additional modeling stances and empirical hypotheses.
+
+## Philosophical Justification
+- From [[S-FT-immediate-datum]], change/experience is given now; denying ongoing change is performatively unstable.
+- CO‑0 alone does not force differentiability; additional assumptions (e.g., bounded Δ or No‑Leap) are needed to rule out jumpy worlds.
+- Keeping ontological truth (ongoing change) distinct from modeling choices prevents overclaiming.
+
+## Clarifications / Further Context
+- Ontology: change-first flow; Gödel pressure marks residual gaps.
+- Modeling stances: metastable patterns, predictive-control framing of consciousness.
+- Empirical hooks: operator drift → resilience; subjective intensity ∝ update gradients; relational observability.
+
+## Next Steps in Chain
+- suggest: add/critique No‑Leap or bounded‑rate assumptions explicitly.
+- suggest: audit consciousness assays and alignment pilots referenced in the source notes.
 
 ## Relationships
 
 - Concepts: [[02_Concepts/C-ontology-of-change]]
+- Parents: [[01_Statements/FoundationalTruth/S-FT-immediate-datum]]
+- Dependencies: [[01_Statements/FoundationalTruth/S-FT-immediate-datum]]
