 # AI_13 comparison protocol for recursive chat experiments
 
 Compares process 1 (`Alice → Bob → Alice`) versus process 2 (`Alice ↔ Bob`) by ensuring symmetric prompts, aligned instruction cards, and drift checks to see which pattern produces faster convergence without hallucinations. Requires controlling for context depth, random seeds, and autocorrelation in queries. Logs outcomes (time, stability, tool usage) to an audit sheet.
+
+## Philosophical Justification
+- Rigorous comparison demands symmetry and drift control; otherwise, observed convergence differences are artifacts.
+- Embedding tool-access drift checks prevents hidden advantage via larger context or tools.
+
+## Clarifications / Further Context
+- Keep prompts/instruction cards symmetric; fix seeds; measure autocorrelation to avoid overcounting.
+- Log time-to-convergence, hallucination rate, and tool usage; compare patterns fairly.
+
+## Next Steps in Chain
+- suggest: fold into [[S-CL-onboarding-gate-liveness]] as standard comparison harness.
