 Every frame, paradigm, or subject-field is surrounded by Gödel holes—structural sites where current tools cannot explain, close, or ground new differences. You cannot ever map the entire metaspace because every location contains unresolved holes and the space itself can never be fully enumerated. This is the perforated, self-modifying metaspace AI_13 describes in lines 1368‑1378; mapping and logging the holes is the only way to know where mutation will be forced next.
+
+## Philosophical Justification
+- From CO-0 and GH framing, closure is local; the metaspace remains perforated by unresolved holes.
+- Recognizing endless perforation prevents overclaiming completeness and guides where novelty will arise.
+
+## Clarifications / Further Context
+- Mapping holes is ongoing; space can reparameterize, so maps must be maintained.
+- Use GH logs to track pressure and likely mutation sites.
+
+## Next Steps in Chain
+- suggest: integrate with [[S-CL-metaspace-shape]] and GH density trackers.
