 # Differential assumptions to include or reject
 
 List of core assumptions to decide on before proceeding: No first change, No minimal Δ (density), No restart after stasis, No absolute frame (gauge-only), Local Lipschitz/causal bounds, and explicit Gödel-hole tracking. Make each explicit so later proofs/constructions can cite them. Default stance: assume a change-bounded rate (or No-Leap) and dense change when pursuing continuity, otherwise allow discrete/hybrid models and keep Gödel tracking alive. This is the scaffolding suggested in AI_13 lines 1484‑1499.
+
+## Philosophical Justification
+- CO’s claims hinge on which refinement/continuity assumptions are accepted; making them explicit prevents hidden premises.
+- Separating optional modules (dense/no-leap/gauge-only) keeps discrete/hybrid models admissible when not committed.
+
+## Clarifications / Further Context
+- Enumerate: No first change; No minimal Δ; No restart; No absolute frame (gauge-only); local Lipschitz/causal bounds; GH tracking.
+- Declare which are in force per derivation; default dense/no-leap only when continuity is required.
+- Keep GH tracking regardless of choice to avoid overclaiming closure.
+
