2026-02-26T20:11:11.994042Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019c9b92-4551-7730-a36c-a30f295a6bf4}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec_command {"cmd":"python - <<'PY'\nimport os, shutil\nroot = \"ChangeOntCode/docs\"\nref = [\n    \"BASELINES.md\",\n    \"BENCHMARKS.md\",\n    \"CO_ALGEBRA\",\n    \"CO_Config_layers.md\",\n    \"CO_CORE_MAP.md\",\n    \"CO_LOGIC.md\",\n    \"CO_MATH.md\",\n    \"CO_RECURSION_PROTOCOL.md\",\n    \"CO_STRICT_RULES.md\",\n    \"demo.md\",\n    \"EVALUATION.md\",\n    \"FND0_IMMEDIATE_DATUM.md\",\n    \"HEADERS.md\",\n    \"KT_Handbook.md\",\n    \"LABELS.md\",\n    \"SPEC_CORE_A_TO_I.md\",\n    \"stoa_bandit.md\",\n    \"stoa_maze.md\",\n    \"stoa_renewal.md\",\n    \"SYMBOLS.md\",\n    # subdirs\n    \"kernel/CO_DiscoveryPolicy.md\",\n    \"kernel/CO_OnticVsPolicy.md\",\n    \"papers/README.md\",\n    \"speccards/CO.K1.Identity.Rtau@v0.2.md\",\n    \"speccards/CO.K2.Lift.Witness@v0.2.md\",\n    \"speccards/CO.K3.Headers.Operational@v0.2.md\",\n    \"speccards/CO.K4.Gauge.RM@v0.2.md\",\n    \"speccards/CO.K5.Logic.ThreeValued@v0.2.md\",\n    \"verification/results.md\",\n    \"verification/spec_map.md\",\n]\n\nhist = [\n    \"Master.md\",\n    \"grouped.md\",\n    \"FREEZE_KERNEL_STOA_RENEWAL.md\",\n    \"FREEZE_STOA_bandit.md\",\n    \"FREEZE_STOA_maze.md\",\n    \"FREEZE_STOA_renewal_phase.md\",\n    \"PREREG.md\",\n    \"ROADMAP.md\",\n    \"OVERVIEW.md\",\n]\n\nmissing = []\nfor lst in (ref, hist):\n    for rel in lst:\n        path = os.path.join(root, rel)\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            missing.append(rel)\n\nif missing:\n    raise SystemExit(f\"Missing files: {missing}\")\n\nfor rel in ref:\n    src = os.path.join(root, rel)\n    dst = os.path.join(root, \"annex/reference\", rel)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)\n    shutil.move(src, dst)\n    # write stub\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(src), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(src, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(f\"Moved to: ChangeOntCode/docs/annex/reference/{rel}\\n\")\n        f.write(\"Non-binding reference.\\n\")\n\nfor rel in hist:\n    src = os.path.join(root, rel)\n    dst = os.path.join(root, \"annex/history\", rel)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)\n    shutil.move(src, dst)\n    # write stub\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(src), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(src, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(f\"Moved to: ChangeOntCode/docs/annex/history/{rel}\\n\")\n        f.write(\"Non-binding history.\\n\")\n\nprint(\"moved\", len(ref)+len(hist))\nPY","yield_time_ms":1000} thread_id=019c9b92-4551-7730-a36c-a30f295a6bf4
2026-02-26T20:11:58.763443Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019c9b92-4551-7730-a36c-a30f295a6bf4}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec_command {"cmd":"cat > ChangeOntCode/docs/00_START_HERE.md <<'EOF'\n# ChangeOnt (Code) — Start Here\n\nThis documentation covers the **code project** under `ChangeOntCode/` only. Theory/FND folders are referenced only as pointers (not duplicated here).\n\n## Authority rules\n- The following pages are the **authoritative spine** (binding for implementation decisions):\n  - `01_RUN_AND_OUTPUTS.md`\n  - `02_ARCHITECTURE_RUNTIME.md`\n  - `03_BINDING_SPEC.md`\n  - `04_ACCEPTANCE_AND_QA.md`\n  - `05_DEV_GUIDE.md`\n  - `06_SPEC_GAPS.md`\n- Anything under `docs/annex/` is **non-binding** reference or history.\n\n## Reading order (recommended)\n1) **How to run and where outputs go** → `01_RUN_AND_OUTPUTS.md`  \n2) **Architecture and runtime path** → `02_ARCHITECTURE_RUNTIME.md`  \n3) **Binding contracts (what must be true)** → `03_BINDING_SPEC.md`  \n4) **Acceptance / QA gate** → `04_ACCEPTANCE_AND_QA.md`  \n5) **Developer guide (how to extend safely)** → `05_DEV_GUIDE.md`  \n6) **Spec gaps (planned vs implemented)** → `06_SPEC_GAPS.md`\n\n## Annex\n- Reference docs: `annex/reference/`\n- Historical/legacy docs: `annex/history/`\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/01_RUN_AND_OUTPUTS.md <<'EOF'\n# Run and Outputs\n\n## Run the suite\nPrimary entrypoint:\n- `python -m experiments.suite_cli --config <path-to-suite-yaml>`\n\nTypical suite configs live under:\n- `ChangeOntCode/experiments/configs/`\n\nThe suite:\n- generates per-run tmp configs under `outputs/suite/tmp/`\n- runs family runners as subprocesses\n- aggregates summaries under `outputs/suite/summary/`\n\n## Run a single family\nExamples:\n- Bandit: `python -m experiments.runners.bandit_runner --config <yaml>`\n- Maze: `python -m experiments.runners.maze_runner --config <yaml>`\n- Renewal: `python -m experiments.runners.renewal_runner --config <yaml>`\n\n## Outputs layout\nOutputs live under:\n- `ChangeOntCode/outputs/suite/<family>/<mode>/<agent>_s<seed>/`\n\nArtifacts include:\n- `metrics.jsonl` — step-wise logs (truth record)\n- `budget.csv` — compute/budget counters (parity)\n- plots (best-effort; may vary by runner)\n- suite summary output under `outputs/suite/summary/`\n\n## metrics.jsonl schema (high level)\nCommon record types:\n- `record_type=\"header\"` — run metadata\n- `metric=\"co_debug\"` — per-step CO telemetry (when CO agent is used)\n- runner/baseline-specific metric records may appear\n\nMinimum required CO telemetry fields (when CO is used):\n- `t` (step index), `action`\n- `signals` (scalar dict), including:\n  - `EC_Identity.same`, `EC_Identity.last_d`\n  - `EB_GHVC.pressure`, `EB_GHVC.mdl_gain`, `EB_GHVC.birth_suggest`\n- mechanism counters (typical): `birth_events`, `merge_events`, `split_events`, `bend_triggers`\n- state sizes (typical): `prototype_count`, `class_count`, `cap_hits`\n- mask info (if present): `translator_mask_mode`, `translator_mask_*`\n\n## Where to look next\n- Architecture/runtime flow: `02_ARCHITECTURE_RUNTIME.md`\n- Binding contracts: `03_BINDING_SPEC.md`\n- QA gate: `04_ACCEPTANCE_AND_QA.md`\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/02_ARCHITECTURE_RUNTIME.md <<'EOF'\n# Architecture and Runtime (Canonical)\n\n## Project structure (code)\nTop-level roles:\n- `environments/` — task worlds (maze/bandit/renewal)\n- `agents/stoa/` — baseline agents (SOTA/standard algorithms)\n- `agents/co/` — CO kernel (primitives/elements/headers/combinators/translators)\n- `experiments/` — harness (suite, runners, logging, plotting)\n- `outputs/` — run artifacts\n\n## Canonical runtime flow (suite)\n1) `experiments/suite_cli.py` loads a suite YAML under `experiments/configs/`\n2) For each job (family × agent × seed):\n   - writes tmp config under `outputs/suite/tmp/...`\n   - calls the family runner as a subprocess\n\nFamily runners:\n- `experiments/runners/bandit_runner.py`\n- `experiments/runners/maze_runner.py`\n- `experiments/runners/renewal_runner.py`\n\nEach runner:\n- constructs environment from `environments/<family>/...`\n- constructs agent (baseline from `agents/stoa/...` or CO)\n- runs the interaction loop and logs metrics\n\n## Canonical CO construction\nCO is built via:\n- `agents/co/integration/core_builder.py::build_co_core(params)`\n  - loads classes from `agents/co/registries/registry.yaml`\n  - instantiates: header, primitives, elements, combinators, translators\n\n## Canonical CO runtime path (binding)\nThe canonical path used by runners is:\n- Adapter select:\n  - `agents/co/adapters/*_adapter.py::select(obs)` → `C_Pipeline.run(...)`\n- Adapter update:\n  - `agents/co/adapters/*_adapter.py::update(feedback)` → `C_Pipeline.run_update(...)`\n- Pipeline:\n  - `agents/co/core/combinators/C_pipeline.py::{run,run_update}`\n- Action selection:\n  - `agents/co/core/elements/action_head.py::ActionHead.step(...)`\n\n**Important:** this canonical path must remain the single source of runtime truth. Alternate/legacy entrypoints must not introduce a second semantics.\n\n## Data flow (at a glance)\n- Environment emits: observation (task-specific), reward/feedback, done\n- Adapter constructs an observation envelope for CO (see `03_BINDING_SPEC.md`)\n- Elements publish:\n  - votes into `co_bus` (vote channels/families)\n  - scalar signals into `co_bus` signal store\n- ActionHead:\n  - drains votes from `co_bus`\n  - consults translator (family-specific scoring and masks)\n  - applies translator mask (blocklist)\n  - blends CO vs classical route based on header state\n\n## Where to look next\n- Contracts (mask, signals, header update ownership): `03_BINDING_SPEC.md`\n- QA gate: `04_ACCEPTANCE_AND_QA.md`\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/03_BINDING_SPEC.md <<'EOF'\n# Binding Spec (Code Contracts)\n\nThis page defines **binding contracts** for implementers. It is intentionally technical and grounded in the canonical runtime.\n\n## 1) Observation envelope (adapter → kernel)\nEvery CO adapter must provide an observation dict containing at minimum:\n- `family`: string (e.g., \"maze\", \"bandit\", \"renewal\")\n- `t`: int step index\nOptional but standardized keys (when available):\n- `episode`: int\n- `feedback`: dict (reward/regret/progress proxies)\n- `translator_mask`: list of blocked actions (blocklist)\n- `probes` / `residuals`: dicts for diagnostics (if runner provides)\n\nAdapters must NOT include hidden env state beyond what the runner already exposes.\n\n## 2) Mask semantics (translator → ActionHead)\nMask mode is **blocklist**:\n- `translator_mask` contains actions that must be forbidden.\n- ActionHead must never select an action present in the blocklist.\nTelemetry should include:\n- `translator_mask_mode=\"blocklist\"`\n- `translator_mask_blocked` (count) or equivalent.\n\n## 3) Vote bus vs scalar signals\n- Votes: stored in `co_bus` by family channel; consumed by ActionHead via drain().\n- Scalar signals: stored in a scalar signal store associated with `co_bus` (e.g., `co_bus.set(key,value)`).\nNaming convention:\n- Use fully qualified keys like `EA_HAQ.novelty`, `EC_Identity.last_d`, `EB_GHVC.pressure`.\n\n## 4) Header update ownership\nHeader update must occur on the **learning/update pass** (pipeline run_update), not on decision pass:\n- Decision pass reads existing header state.\n- Update pass updates header using outcome/feedback.\n\n## 5) Required CO telemetry (minimum)\nWhen CO is used, per-step logs must include:\n- `t`, `action`\n- `signals` dict containing at minimum:\n  - `EC_Identity.same`, `EC_Identity.last_d`\n  - `EB_GHVC.pressure`, `EB_GHVC.mdl_gain`, `EB_GHVC.birth_suggest`\n- Mechanism counters when relevant:\n  - `birth_events`, `merge_events`, `split_events`, `bend_triggers`\n- State sizes:\n  - `prototype_count`, `class_count`, `cap_hits` (as available)\n\n## 6) No duplicate runtime semantics\nThere must be exactly one canonical runtime semantics (adapters → pipeline.run/run_update). Any alternate paths must be clearly marked non-canonical and must not diverge.\n\n## Where to look next\n- QA gate and acceptance: `04_ACCEPTANCE_AND_QA.md`\n- Spec gaps / missing referenced modules: `06_SPEC_GAPS.md`\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/04_ACCEPTANCE_AND_QA.md <<'EOF'\n# Acceptance and QA\n\n## QA gate\nThe QA gate script is:\n- `ChangeOntCode/tools/qa.sh`\n\nIt must pass before accepting changes to kernel/harness/doc contracts.\n\n## What qa.sh checks (high level)\n- header update occurs exactly once per env step (and originates from update pass)\n- scalar signals exist and are logged\n- identity varies (same sometimes 0; last_d sometimes >0)\n- GHVC birth suggests and causes state mutation (birth_count or prototype_count changes)\n- mask contract is not violated\n- co_debug record is present once per t\n\n## How to run\nFrom repo root (or ChangeOntCode root as appropriate):\n- `bash ChangeOntCode/tools/qa.sh`\n\n## Smoke runs (recommended)\nFixed seeds (0/1/2) for bandit and maze using existing runner configs.\n\n## If QA fails\n- Do not “paper over” failures by changing docs.\n- Fix the implementation or correct the binding contract (only if contract was wrong).\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/05_DEV_GUIDE.md <<'EOF'\n# Developer Guide (Code)\n\n## Lanes (avoid conflicts)\n- Kernel (`agents/co/`): primitives, elements, headers, combinators, translators\n- Harness (`experiments/`): suite, runners, configs, plotting, logging\n- Envs (`environments/`): task worlds\n- Baselines (`agents/stoa/`): STOA agents\n- Docs (`docs/`): spine is binding, annex is non-binding\n\n## Add a new environment (high-level)\n1) Create env under `environments/<family>/...`\n2) Add a runner config under `experiments/configs/`\n3) Ensure runner exposes only legal observation envelope keys\n4) Add translator if required under `agents/co/integration/translators/`\n5) Add/verify baselines if relevant under `agents/stoa/`\n6) Run suite + QA\n\n## Add a new baseline (STOA)\n1) Implement baseline agent under `agents/stoa/<family>/...`\n2) Register in the family runner baseline switch\n3) Ensure budgets/logs comparable\n4) Run suite + QA\n\n## Add/modify a CO element or primitive\nRules:\n- Elements must call primitives rather than re-implementing the same logic privately.\n- Elements must publish votes to bus and scalar signals to signal store using stable keys.\n- All changes must keep canonical runtime path intact and pass QA.\n\n## Where to look next\n- Runtime architecture: `02_ARCHITECTURE_RUNTIME.md`\n- Binding contracts: `03_BINDING_SPEC.md`\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/06_SPEC_GAPS.md <<'EOF'\n# Spec Gaps (Docs vs Code)\n\nThis page tracks missing or aspirational features referenced by docs that are not present in the codebase. **Do not implement features just because they appear here**; treat them as planned gaps.\n\n## Missing files referenced by older docs (examples)\nThe following paths are referenced in some annex/reference docs but do not exist in the codebase (as of current snapshot):\n- `core/headers/collapse.py`\n- `core/headers/meta_flip.py`\n- `core/quotient/equivalence.py`\n- `core/quotient/infimum_lift.py`\n- `evaluation/invariance_test.py`\n- `tests/test_lift.py`\n- `tests/test_logic.py`\n\n## Moved paths (docs need redirects)\nSome older docs reference outdated paths. Use the canonical paths:\n- Registry: `agents/co/registries/registry.yaml`\n- CO builder: `agents/co/integration/core_builder.py`\n- Translators: `agents/co/integration/translators/`\n\n## Duplicates (archived)\nThe following docs are historical/legacy and should remain under `annex/history/`:\n- `Master.md`\n- `grouped.md`\n- `FREEZE_*` docs\n\n## Policy\n- Binding truth lives in spine pages only.\n- Annex docs may contain aspirational specs; treat them as reference/history unless explicitly upgraded into binding spec.\nEOF\n","yield_time_ms":1000} thread_id=019c9b92-4551-7730-a36c-a30f295a6bf4
2026-02-26T20:12:26.796274Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019c9b92-4551-7730-a36c-a30f295a6bf4}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec_command {"cmd":"mkdir -p ChangeOntCode/tools\ncat > ChangeOntCode/tools/qa.sh <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# --- select metrics.jsonl (mtime preferred, lexicographic fallback) ---\nLATEST_METRICS=\"$(\npython - <<'PY'\nimport os, glob\npaths = glob.glob(\"ChangeOntCode/outputs/**/metrics.jsonl\", recursive=True)\npaths = sorted(paths, key=lambda p: os.path.getmtime(p))\nprint(paths[-1] if paths else \"\")\nPY\n)\"\nif [ -z \"$LATEST_METRICS\" ]; then\n  if command -v rg >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    LATEST_METRICS=\"$(rg --files -g 'metrics.jsonl' ChangeOntCode/outputs | sort | tail -n 1)\"\n  else\n    LATEST_METRICS=\"\"\n  fi\nfi\necho \"LATEST_METRICS=$LATEST_METRICS\"\ntest -n \"$LATEST_METRICS\"\n\nFAILS=()\n\nfail() {\n  local name=\"$1\" msg=\"$2\" excerpt_cmd=\"$3\"\n  echo \"FAIL: $name\"\n  echo \"  $msg\"\n  echo \"  Excerpt (first 5):\"\n  eval \"$excerpt_cmd\" | head -n 5 || true\n  FAILS+=(\"$name\")\n}\n\npass() { echo \"PASS: $1\"; }\n\n# 1) JSONL header present\nif jq -e 'select(.record_type==\"header\" and .runner!=null and .agent!=null)' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" >/dev/null; then\n  pass \"header_present\"\nelse\n  fail \"header_present\" \"Missing header record with record_type/runner/agent\" \\\n    \"jq -c 'select(.record_type==\\\"header\\\")' \\\"$LATEST_METRICS\\\"\"\nfi\n\n# 2) header update exactly once per t\nBAD_T=\"$(jq -r 'select(.header_update_count!=null) | .t' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" | sort -n | uniq -c | awk '$1!=1{print $2}' | head -n 1)\"\nif [ -z \"$BAD_T\" ]; then\n  pass \"header_update_once\"\nelse\n  fail \"header_update_once\" \"t with count != 1 detected\" \\\n    \"jq -c 'select(.header_update_count!=null and .t==$BAD_T)' \\\"$LATEST_METRICS\\\"\"\nfi\n\n# 3) header update source is run_update only\nBAD_SRC=\"$(jq -r 'select(.header_update_source!=null) | .header_update_source' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" | sort | uniq -c | awk '$2!=\"run_update\"{print $2; exit}')\"\nif [ -z \"$BAD_SRC\" ]; then\n  pass \"header_update_source\"\nelse\n  fail \"header_update_source\" \"Non-run_update source detected: $BAD_SRC\" \\\n    \"jq -c 'select(.header_update_source!=null and .header_update_source!=\\\"run_update\\\")' \\\"$LATEST_METRICS\\\"\"\nfi\n\n# 4) scalar signals present\nif jq -e 'select(.signals!=null and\n  .signals[\"EC_Identity.same\"]!=null and\n  .signals[\"EC_Identity.last_d\"]!=null and\n  .signals[\"EB_GHVC.pressure\"]!=null and\n  .signals[\"EB_GHVC.mdl_gain\"]!=null and\n  .signals[\"EB_GHVC.birth_suggest\"]!=null)' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" >/dev/null; then\n  pass \"signals_present\"\nelse\n  fail \"signals_present\" \"signals missing required keys\" \\\n    \"jq -c 'select(.signals!=null)' \\\"$LATEST_METRICS\\\"\"\nfi\n\n# 5) identity_ok varies; last_d > 0 exists\nHAS_ZERO=\"$(jq -r 'select(.signals!=null) | .signals[\"EC_Identity.same\"]' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" | awk '$1==0{print; exit}')\"\nHAS_ONE=\"$(jq -r 'select(.signals!=null) | .signals[\"EC_Identity.same\"]' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" | awk '$1==1{print; exit}')\"\nHAS_LASTD=\"$(jq -r 'select(.signals!=null and (.signals[\"EC_Identity.last_d\"]|tonumber)>0) | .t' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" | head -n 1)\"\nif [ -n \"$HAS_ZERO\" ] && [ -n \"$HAS_ONE\" ] && [ -n \"$HAS_LASTD\" ]; then\n  pass \"identity_variation\"\nelse\n  fail \"identity_variation\" \"identity_ok not varying or last_d never > 0\" \\\n    \"jq -c 'select(.signals!=null) | {t:.t,same:.signals[\\\"EC_Identity.same\\\"],last_d:.signals[\\\"EC_Identity.last_d\\\"]}' \\\"$LATEST_METRICS\\\"\"\nfi\n\n# 6) GHVC birth suggests + count changes\nHAS_BIRTH=\"$(jq -r 'select(.signals!=null and .signals[\"EB_GHVC.birth_suggest\"]==1) | .t' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" | head -n 1)\"\nBIRTH_CHG=\"$(jq -r 'select(.birth_count!=null) | .birth_count' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" | sort -n | uniq -c | wc -l | awk '$1>1{print}')\"\nif [ -n \"$HAS_BIRTH\" ] && [ -n \"$BIRTH_CHG\" ]; then\n  pass \"ghvc_birth\"\nelse\n  fail \"ghvc_birth\" \"No birth_suggest==1 or birth_count not changing\" \\\n    \"jq -c 'select(.signals!=null or .birth_count!=null) | {t:.t,birth_suggest:.signals[\\\"EB_GHVC.birth_suggest\\\"],birth_count:.birth_count}' \\\"$LATEST_METRICS\\\"\"\nfi\n\n# 7) mask semantics (allowlist or blocklist)\nBAD_MASK=\"$(jq -r '\n  if .translator_mask!=null and .mask_mode==\"allowlist\" then\n    ((.translator_mask|index(.action))==null)\n  elif .translator_mask!=null and .mask_mode==\"blocklist\" then\n    ((.translator_mask|index(.action))!=null)\n  else false end\n  | select(.) | .t' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" | head -n 1)\"\nif [ -z \"$BAD_MASK\" ]; then\n  pass \"mask_semantics\"\nelse\n  fail \"mask_semantics\" \"Mask contract violated at t=$BAD_MASK\" \\\n    \"jq -c 'select(.translator_mask!=null and .t==$BAD_MASK) | {t:.t,mode:.mask_mode,action:.action,mask:.translator_mask}' \\\"$LATEST_METRICS\\\"\"\nfi\n\n# 8) co_debug once per t\nBAD_T2=\"$(jq -r 'select(.metric==\"co_debug\") | .t' \"$LATEST_METRICS\" | sort -n | uniq -c | awk '$1!=1{print $2}' | head -n 1)\"\nif [ -z \"$BAD_T2\" ]; then\n  pass \"co_debug_once\"\nelse\n  fail \"co_debug_once\" \"co_debug count != 1 at t=$BAD_T2\" \\\n    \"jq -c 'select(.metric==\\\"co_debug\\\" and .t==$BAD_T2)' \\\"$LATEST_METRICS\\\"\"\nfi\n\necho\nif [ \"${#FAILS[@]}\" -eq 0 ]; then\n  echo \"PASS: all checks\"\n  exit 0\nelse\n  echo \"FAIL: ${#FAILS[@]} check(s) failed -> ${FAILS[*]}\"\n  exit 1\nfi\nEOF\nchmod +x ChangeOntCode/tools/qa.sh\n","yield_time_ms":1000} thread_id=019c9b92-4551-7730-a36c-a30f295a6bf4
