2026-02-26T22:47:12.613084Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019c9b92-4551-7730-a36c-a30f295a6bf4}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec_command {"cmd":"mkdir -p ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/{04_PRIMITIVES,05_ELEMENTS,06_HEADERS,07_COMBINATORS,08_TRANSLATORS,09_ACCEPTANCE}\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/00_INDEX.md <<'EOF'\n# Kernel Spec Index\n\n## Table of Contents\n1. `01_KERNEL_RUNTIME.md`\n2. `02_DATA_CONTRACTS.md`\n3. `03_WIRING_MAP.md`\n4. `04_PRIMITIVES/`\n5. `05_ELEMENTS/`\n6. `06_HEADERS/`\n7. `07_COMBINATORS/`\n8. `08_TRANSLATORS/`\n9. `09_ACCEPTANCE/`\n\n## Docs -> Code Rule\n- These kernel specs are **binding** and must match the runtime implemented under `ChangeOntCode/agents/co/` and `ChangeOntCode/experiments/`.\n- If a spec conflicts with code, update code to comply or add a TODO in `09_ACCEPTANCE/SPEC_GAPS.md` describing the mismatch and required decision.\n\n## Implementation Order (Recommended)\n1. `07_COMBINATORS/C_Pipeline.md` (defines canonical runtime and update semantics)\n2. `02_DATA_CONTRACTS.md` (observation/mask/signal contracts)\n3. `05_ELEMENTS/ActionHead.md` (final action + telemetry surface)\n4. `05_ELEMENTS/EC_Identity.md` and `05_ELEMENTS/EB_GHVC.md` (required signals)\n5. `04_PRIMITIVES/P1_BendMetric.md`, `P12_ClosureQuotient.md`, `P10_ChangeOpsCore.md` (support identity + GHVC state)\n6. `08_TRANSLATORS/*` (family-specific scoring and masks)\n7. Remaining elements/primitives/headers\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/01_KERNEL_RUNTIME.md <<'EOF'\n# Kernel Runtime (Canonical)\n\n## Canonical Flow (Files and Calls)\n1. Suite entry: `experiments/suite_cli.py`\n2. Runner: `experiments/runners/{bandit,maze,renewal}_runner.py`\n3. CO adapter: `agents/co/adapters/*_adapter.py`\n4. Core builder: `agents/co/integration/core_builder.py::build_co_core`\n5. Pipeline: `agents/co/core/combinators/C_pipeline.py::{run,run_update}`\n6. Elements: `agents/co/core/elements/*`\n7. ActionHead: `agents/co/core/elements/action_head.py::ActionHead.step`\n8. Translator: `agents/co/integration/translators/*_translator.py`\n9. Logs: `experiments/logging/logging.py::write_metric_line`\n\n## Header Update Ownership\n- Header updates occur **only** in `C_Pipeline.run_update(...)`.\n- The decision pass `C_Pipeline.run(...)` reads header state but must not call `header.update`.\n\n## Votes and Signals\n- Votes are stored in `co_bus` and drained once per decision step.\n- Scalar signals are stored in `co_bus` and snapshotted by ActionHead into the `signals` dict.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/02_DATA_CONTRACTS.md <<'EOF'\n# Data Contracts\n\n## Observation Envelope (Global)\nRequired keys:\n- `family: str`\n- `t: int`\n\nOptional keys:\n- `episode: int`\n- `feedback: dict`\n- `translator_mask: list`\n- `residuals: dict`\n- `probes: dict`\n- `history: list`\n- `trace: list`\n- `action_space: list`\n\n## Mask Semantics\n- Mask is a **blocklist**. Any action in `translator_mask` must be excluded from CO scores before blending.\n\n## Vote Bus vs Scalar Signals\n- Votes: `co_bus.push(family, action, weight, ...)` and `co_bus.drain(family)`.\n- Signals: `co_bus.set(key, value)` or `bus[key] = value`. ActionHead snapshots `co_bus.signals()`.\n\n## Telemetry Schema (Essentials)\n- `metrics.jsonl` is JSONL. CO records use `metric=\"co_debug\"`.\n- Canonical signals keys:\n  - `signals[\"EC_Identity.same\"]`\n  - `signals[\"EC_Identity.last_d\"]`\n  - `signals[\"EB_GHVC.pressure\"]`\n  - `signals[\"EB_GHVC.mdl_gain\"]`\n  - `signals[\"EB_GHVC.birth_suggest\"]`\n- Canonical top-level fields when present:\n  - `birth_count`, `header_update_count`, `header_update_source`, `mask_mode`, `translator_mask`\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/03_WIRING_MAP.md <<'EOF'\n# Wiring Map\n\n## Elements -> Primitives -> Signals (Current Implementation)\n- `EA_HAQ` -> uses primitives (history/EMA logic) and publishes `EA_HAQ.novelty` (if present)\n- `EB_GHVC` -> uses `P10_ChangeOpsCore` (birth), `P12_ClosureQuotient` (classes), publishes:\n  - `EB_GHVC.pressure`, `EB_GHVC.mdl_gain`, `EB_GHVC.birth_suggest`\n  - `birth_events`, `merge_events`, `split_events`, `prototype_count`, `class_count`, `cap_hits`, `birth_count`\n- `EC_Identity` -> uses `P1_BendMetric` + `P12_ClosureQuotient`, publishes:\n  - `EC_Identity.same`, `EC_Identity.last_d`, `bend_triggers`, `class_count`\n- `EG_DensityPrecision` -> uses visit tracking, publishes `EG_DensityPrecision.visit_density`\n- `VoteBridge` -> publishes votes to `co_bus`\n- `ActionHead` -> drains votes, applies translator masks, blends scores, emits `signals` snapshot\n\n## Planned vs Implemented\n- Implemented: `EA_HAQ`, `EB_GHVC`, `EC_Identity`, `EG_DensityPrecision`, `VoteBridge`, `ActionHead`\n- Planned (see `09_ACCEPTANCE/SPEC_GAPS.md`): advanced quotient / equivalence / infimum_lift, meta_flip, collapse, invariance tests\n\nEOF\n\n# ---- PRIMITIVES ----\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/04_PRIMITIVES/P1_BendMetric.md <<'EOF'\n# P1_BendMetric\n\n## Purpose\nCompute bend distance between traces and support equivalence closure.\n\n## Inputs (exact keys/types; where read from)\n- `trace: list|tuple` from observation `history` or `trace`\n- `eps: float` from header state (`header.state.eps_eff` if present)\n\n## Outputs (exact vote families, signals keys, return dict fields)\n- Returns numeric bend distance values for identity checks (used inside EC_Identity)\n\n## State mutation (what is allowed to change; where state is stored)\n- No global state. Pure function behavior.\n\n## Algorithm (step-by-step; include constants/thresholds if binding)\n1. Compute distance between traces.\n2. Compare to epsilon for identity match.\n\n## Forbidden (explicit anti-smuggling rules)\n- Must not read hidden environment state.\n- Must not mutate shared state.\n\n## Telemetry (exact metrics.jsonl / co_debug fields and signals dict keys)\n- Telemetry emitted by EC_Identity: `signals[\"EC_Identity.same\"]`, `signals[\"EC_Identity.last_d\"]`.\n\n## Acceptance (exact reviewer procedure: which smoke run, which qa.sh checks, what evidence line(s) prove it)\n- Run `outputs/verify/configs/qa_maze.yaml` and `qa_bandit.yaml`.\n- `qa.sh` must pass `signals_present` and `identity_variation`.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/04_PRIMITIVES/P2_Gauge.md <<'EOF'\n# P2_Gauge\n\n## Purpose\nProvide gauge update utilities for HAQ-style modulation.\n\n## Inputs (exact keys/types; where read from)\n- Observation history and optional signals (as defined by element using it).\n\n## Outputs (exact vote families, signals keys, return dict fields)\n- Element-local values for HAQ gating; no direct signals mandated.\n\n## State mutation (what is allowed to change; where state is stored)\n- Internal gauge state stored in primitive instance if implemented.\n\n## Algorithm (step-by-step; include constants/thresholds if binding)\n- TODO: Exact gauge update equations are not defined in current code. Must be decided if/when P2 is implemented.\n\n## Forbidden (explicit anti-smuggling rules)\n- Must not write to co_bus signals directly; only elements publish signals.\n\n## Telemetry (exact metrics.jsonl / co_debug fields and signals dict keys)\n- None directly; via element that consumes it.\n\n## Acceptance (exact reviewer procedure: which smoke run, which qa.sh checks, what evidence line(s) prove it)\n- Not currently gated by QA; verify element-level telemetry in HAQ if implemented.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/04_PRIMITIVES/P3_MDL.md <<'EOF'\n# P3_MDL\n\n## Purpose\nCompute MDL-style penalty or gain for model complexity changes.\n\n## Inputs (exact keys/types; where read from)\n- Residual/error proxy and model size parameters (element-provided).\n\n## Outputs (exact vote families, signals keys, return dict fields)\n- MDL gain value for GHVC decision logic.\n\n## State mutation (what is allowed to change; where state is stored)\n- Primitive-local state only.\n\n## Algorithm (step-by-step; include constants/thresholds if binding)\n- In code, GHVC uses `mdl_gain = max(0, mse) - lambda * k_new`.\n\n## Forbidden (explicit anti-smuggling rules)\n- Must not create prototypes or mutate P10 directly.\n\n## Telemetry (exact metrics.jsonl / co_debug fields and signals dict keys)\n- `signals[\"EB_GHVC.mdl_gain\"]` emitted by GHVC.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `qa.sh` must pass `signals_present` and `ghvc_birth` when QA variant used.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/04_PRIMITIVES/P7_Precision.md <<'EOF'\n# P7_Precision\n\n## Purpose\nPrecision/density scheduling for rounding or signal compression.\n\n## Inputs\n- Observation stats from element (density/visit stats).\n\n## Outputs\n- Precision schedule or rounding value consumed by element.\n\n## State mutation\n- Primitive-local state only.\n\n## Algorithm\n- TODO: exact precision update rules are not defined in current code; element owns behavior.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not publish signals directly.\n\n## Telemetry\n- Via `EG_DensityPrecision` signals (if implemented).\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not required by QA; verify through element telemetry if added.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/04_PRIMITIVES/P9_VariableBirth.md <<'EOF'\n# P9_VariableBirth\n\n## Purpose\nLegacy placeholder for variable-birth logic (not directly used in current GHVC path).\n\n## Inputs\n- TODO: Not implemented in current runtime; see `agents/co/core/primitives/P9_variable_birth` if added.\n\n## Outputs\n- Not used in canonical path.\n\n## State mutation\n- TODO: Not implemented.\n\n## Algorithm\n- TODO: Not implemented.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not be required for QA.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not required; see `09_ACCEPTANCE/SPEC_GAPS.md`.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/04_PRIMITIVES/P10_ChangeOpsCore.md <<'EOF'\n# P10_ChangeOpsCore\n\n## Purpose\nMaintain prototype list for GHVC variable births and change-ops core state.\n\n## Inputs\n- Birth acceptance signal from GHVC.\n- Optional history/trace from observation.\n\n## Outputs\n- Prototype list (used to compute `prototype_count` and classes).\n\n## State mutation\n- Mutates `primitives[\"P10\"].prototypes` when a birth is accepted.\n\n## Algorithm\n1. If GHVC indicates `born_variable`, ensure `P10` exists.\n2. Append a prototype (from history trace if available, else a unique token).\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not accept births without GHVC gating.\n\n## Telemetry\n- GHVC publishes `prototype_count` and derived `merge_events`/`split_events`.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `qa.sh` must pass `ghvc_birth` when QA configs are used.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/04_PRIMITIVES/P12_ClosureQuotient.md <<'EOF'\n# P12_ClosureQuotient\n\n## Purpose\nCompute equivalence classes over prototypes using bend distance.\n\n## Inputs\n- Prototype list from P10\n- Bend distance from P1\n\n## Outputs\n- Class list used to compute `class_count` and merge counts.\n\n## State mutation\n- None (pure computation), but primitive instance may cache epsilon.\n\n## Algorithm\n- Use closure over prototypes under bend distance threshold.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not mutate prototypes.\n\n## Telemetry\n- `class_count` emitted by GHVC.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Indirectly via `qa.sh` ghvc_birth and signals.\n\nEOF\n\n# ---- ELEMENTS ----\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/05_ELEMENTS/EA_HAQ.md <<'EOF'\n# EA_HAQ\n\n## Purpose\nHistory-adaptive gating of CO behavior (novelty/density hints for translators).\n\n## Inputs (exact keys/types; where read from)\n- Observation history/trace from `history` or `trace`.\n\n## Outputs (exact vote families, signals keys, return dict fields)\n- May publish `EA_HAQ.novelty` into `signals`.\n\n## State mutation (what is allowed to change; where state is stored)\n- Element-local history/EMA state only.\n\n## Algorithm (step-by-step; include constants/thresholds if binding)\n- Maintains EMA over recent observations; publishes novelty scalar.\n\n## Forbidden (explicit anti-smuggling rules)\n- Must not mutate header state directly.\n\n## Telemetry (exact metrics.jsonl / co_debug fields and signals dict keys)\n- `signals[\"EA_HAQ.novelty\"]` (if published).\n\n## Acceptance (exact reviewer procedure: which smoke run, which qa.sh checks, what evidence line(s) prove it)\n- Not required by QA; visible in `signals` dict for CO runs.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/05_ELEMENTS/EB_GHVC.md <<'EOF'\n# EB_GHVC\n\n## Purpose\nBirth suggestion and variable creation based on residual/probe signals.\n\n## Inputs (exact keys/types; where read from)\n- `residuals: dict` and `probes: dict` from observation.\n- Fallback: `feedback.reward` when residuals/probes absent.\n- Uses header epsilon and primitive budget if present.\n\n## Outputs (exact vote families, signals keys, return dict fields)\n- Signals:\n  - `signals[\"EB_GHVC.pressure\"]`\n  - `signals[\"EB_GHVC.mdl_gain\"]`\n  - `signals[\"EB_GHVC.birth_suggest\"]`\n- Counters:\n  - `birth_events`, `merge_events`, `split_events`, `prototype_count`, `class_count`, `cap_hits`, `birth_count`\n\n## State mutation (what is allowed to change; where state is stored)\n- May create/update `primitives[\"P10\"]` and `primitives[\"P12\"]`.\n- Updates `primitives[\"birth_count\"]` monotonic counter.\n\n## Algorithm (step-by-step; include constants/thresholds if binding)\n1. Compute `pressure` from residuals/probes; fallback uses `abs(reward)*4.5`.\n2. Compute `mdl_gain = max(0, mse) - lam_mdl*k_new`.\n3. Accept birth if `pressure > gamma` and `mdl_gain > 0` and budget allows.\n4. If accepted, append prototype to P10 and update closure/class counts.\n\n## Forbidden (explicit anti-smuggling rules)\n- Must not emit votes; GHVC is signal-only.\n\n## Telemetry (exact metrics.jsonl / co_debug fields and signals dict keys)\n- Required: `signals[\"EB_GHVC.pressure\"]`, `signals[\"EB_GHVC.mdl_gain\"]`, `signals[\"EB_GHVC.birth_suggest\"]`.\n- Required counters in `co_debug` when present: `birth_count`, `birth_events`, `prototype_count`.\n\n## Acceptance (exact reviewer procedure: which smoke run, which qa.sh checks, what evidence line(s) prove it)\n- Run `outputs/verify/configs/qa_bandit.yaml` or `qa_maze.yaml`.\n- `qa.sh` must pass `signals_present` and `ghvc_birth`.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/05_ELEMENTS/EC_Identity.md <<'EOF'\n# EC_Identity\n\n## Purpose\nIdentity via bend-distance equivalence over short traces.\n\n## Inputs (exact keys/types; where read from)\n- `history` or `trace` from observation.\n- `eps` from header state (`header.state.eps_eff` if present).\n\n## Outputs (exact vote families, signals keys, return dict fields)\n- Signals:\n  - `signals[\"EC_Identity.same\"]`\n  - `signals[\"EC_Identity.last_d\"]`\n- Counter: `bend_triggers`\n\n## State mutation (what is allowed to change; where state is stored)\n- Updates `primitives[\"identity_mem\"]` trace memory.\n\n## Algorithm (step-by-step; include constants/thresholds if binding)\n1. Build trace from `history` or `trace` (window length `trace_len`).\n2. Compute bend distance to previous traces; set `identity_ok` if `last_d <= eps`.\n3. Publish signals and update memory.\n\n## Forbidden (explicit anti-smuggling rules)\n- Must not mutate environment state.\n\n## Telemetry (exact metrics.jsonl / co_debug fields and signals dict keys)\n- Required: `signals[\"EC_Identity.same\"]`, `signals[\"EC_Identity.last_d\"]`.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `qa.sh` must pass `signals_present` and `identity_variation`.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/05_ELEMENTS/EG_DensityPrecision.md <<'EOF'\n# EG_DensityPrecision\n\n## Purpose\nTrack visit density and precision hints for translators.\n\n## Inputs\n- Observation coordinates and visit history (maze).\n\n## Outputs\n- Signal: `EG_DensityPrecision.visit_density` (if implemented)\n\n## State mutation\n- Uses `visit_tracker` primitive state.\n\n## Algorithm\n- Updates visit statistics and emits density scalar.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not decide actions directly.\n\n## Telemetry\n- Visible in `signals` dict.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not required by QA; verify presence in `signals` for maze runs.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/05_ELEMENTS/EH_BreadthDepth.md <<'EOF'\n# EH_BreadthDepth\n\n## Purpose\nBreadth-depth scheduling (legacy; not on critical path in current QA).\n\n## Inputs\n- Loopiness or visit-density signals.\n\n## Outputs\n- Optional votes or signals (not required by QA).\n\n## State mutation\n- Element-local counters.\n\n## Algorithm\n- TODO: Exact scheduling policy not defined in current code.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not bypass ActionHead.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None required.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not gated by QA.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/05_ELEMENTS/EF_Router.md <<'EOF'\n# EF_Router\n\n## Purpose\nHeader/router element for CO vs classical routing (legacy in current code).\n\n## Inputs\n- Header state and signals.\n\n## Outputs\n- Potential route signals (not required by QA).\n\n## State mutation\n- Header state updates are **not** allowed here (run_update only).\n\n## Algorithm\n- TODO: Router behavior not defined in current code.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not select actions directly.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None required.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not gated by QA.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/05_ELEMENTS/VoteBridge.md <<'EOF'\n# VoteBridge\n\n## Purpose\nTranslate element scores into co_bus votes.\n\n## Inputs\n- Element-local scores or signals.\n\n## Outputs\n- Votes: `co_bus.push(family, action, weight, source=...)`.\n\n## State mutation\n- Writes to `co_bus` vote store only.\n\n## Algorithm\n- Push weighted votes into family channel.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not drain votes or select actions.\n\n## Telemetry\n- Indirect via ActionHead `co_bus_votes` count.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not directly gated by QA; visible in co_debug `co_bus_votes`.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/05_ELEMENTS/ActionHead.md <<'EOF'\n# ActionHead\n\n## Purpose\nDrain votes, apply translator mask, blend CO and classical scores, and emit final action + telemetry.\n\n## Inputs (exact keys/types; where read from)\n- Observation dict (includes `family`, `t`, and optional `action_space`).\n- `co_bus` for votes and signals.\n- Translator output `(scores, translator_mask, info)`.\n\n## Outputs (exact vote families, signals keys, return dict fields)\n- `action`: final action\n- `co_policy`, `co_weight`, `classic_weight`, `co_bus_votes`, `co_sources`\n- `signals` dict snapshot (must include canonical signals keys)\n- Counters: `birth_count`, `birth_events`, `merge_events`, `split_events`, `bend_triggers`, `prototype_count`, `class_count`, `cap_hits`\n\n## State mutation (what is allowed to change; where state is stored)\n- Maintains ActionHead local history (for oscillation breaking).\n- Does not mutate header or primitives besides reading from co_bus.\n\n## Algorithm (step-by-step; include constants/thresholds if binding)\n1. Drain votes from `co_bus` for this family.\n2. Call translator to get `trans_scores` and `translator_mask` (blocklist).\n3. Fuse vote scores and translator scores; normalize.\n4. Apply blocklist mask to CO scores.\n5. Compute classical scores (family-specific fallback).\n6. Blend CO vs classical by `co_weight`.\n7. Select best action; apply maze anti-oscillation guardrails.\n8. Attach telemetry and return.\n\n## Forbidden (explicit anti-smuggling rules)\n- Must not call `header.update`.\n- Must not drain votes more than once per step.\n\n## Telemetry (exact metrics.jsonl / co_debug fields and signals dict keys)\n- `signals` dict must include canonical keys listed in `02_DATA_CONTRACTS.md`.\n- Derived convenience fields (allowed but non-canonical): `identity_ok`, `last_d`, `ghvc_pressure`, `ghvc_mdl_gain`.\n\n## Acceptance (exact reviewer procedure: which smoke run, which qa.sh checks, what evidence line(s) prove it)\n- Run `outputs/verify/configs/qa_bandit.yaml` and `qa_maze.yaml`.\n- `qa.sh` must pass all checks.\n\nEOF\n\n# ---- HEADERS ----\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/06_HEADERS/H_SSI.md <<'EOF'\n# H_SSI\n\n## Purpose\nSelf-situated inference header (default for CO).\n\n## Inputs\n- Observation envelope in `run_update`.\n\n## Outputs\n- Header state used by ActionHead (e.g., `co_weight`).\n\n## State mutation\n- Header state may mutate only in `run_update`.\n\n## Algorithm\n- TODO: Exact SSI update rules are not defined in current code; header implementation governs behavior.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not be updated in decision pass.\n\n## Telemetry\n- Exposed indirectly via `debug_header_updates` if enabled.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `qa.sh` checks header update source when present.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/06_HEADERS/H_CS.md <<'EOF'\n# H_CS\n\n## Purpose\nClassical-slice header (CO off).\n\n## Inputs\n- Observation envelope in `run_update`.\n\n## Outputs\n- Header state indicating classical mode.\n\n## State mutation\n- Update only in `run_update`.\n\n## Algorithm\n- TODO: Exact classical-slice logic defined in header implementation.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not affect decision pass outside ActionHead blend.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None required.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not part of QA smoke path unless configured.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/06_HEADERS/H_ID.md <<'EOF'\n# H_ID\n\n## Purpose\nIdentity-first header (fixed epsilon).\n\n## Inputs\n- Observation envelope in `run_update`.\n\n## Outputs\n- Header state with fixed epsilon/identity policy.\n\n## State mutation\n- Update only in `run_update`.\n\n## Algorithm\n- TODO: Exact H_ID policy defined in header implementation.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not update in decision pass.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None required.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not part of QA smoke path unless configured.\n\nEOF\n\n# ---- COMBINATORS ----\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/07_COMBINATORS/C_Pipeline.md <<'EOF'\n# C_Pipeline\n\n## Purpose\nCanonical runtime combinator for decision and update passes.\n\n## Inputs\n- `elements: list`\n- `primitives: dict`\n- `header`\n- `observation: dict`\n- `feedback: dict | None`\n\n## Outputs\n- Aggregated dict output from elements and ActionHead.\n\n## State mutation\n- Update pass calls `header.update` and element `update` methods.\n- Decision pass calls element `update`, `step`, `metrics` except ActionHead, then ActionHead.step once.\n\n## Algorithm\n- `run`:\n  1. Iterate elements except ActionHead: call `update`, `step`, `metrics` if present.\n  2. Call ActionHead.step once and return its output merged.\n- `run_update`:\n  1. Call `header.update` with observation (+ feedback in `feedback` field).\n  2. Call element `update` (no `step`), skip ActionHead.\n\n## Forbidden\n- No header updates in `run`.\n- No ActionHead calls in `run_update`.\n\n## Telemetry\n- Indirectly via ActionHead output.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `qa.sh` `header_update_source` must be `run_update` when present.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/07_COMBINATORS/C_Gate.md <<'EOF'\n# C_Gate\n\n## Purpose\nOptional gating combinator for routing elements (not required in QA).\n\n## Inputs\n- Element outputs + header state.\n\n## Outputs\n- Routed element outputs.\n\n## State mutation\n- None.\n\n## Algorithm\n- TODO: Not defined in current code.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not create alternate runtime path.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None required.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not gated by QA.\n\nEOF\n\n# ---- TRANSLATORS ----\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/08_TRANSLATORS/bandit_translator.md <<'EOF'\n# Bandit Translator\n\n## Purpose\nConvert bandit stats into action scores and mask (blocklist).\n\n## Inputs (exact keys/types; where read from)\n- `n_arms: int` from observation\n- `t: int` from observation\n- `bandit_stats` primitive\n\n## Outputs (exact vote families, signals keys, return dict fields)\n- `(scores: Dict[int,float], translator_mask: set, info: dict)`\n- `translator_mask` is a blocklist (usually empty for bandit)\n\n## State mutation\n- None.\n\n## Algorithm\n- UCB-style scores using counts/means from `bandit_stats` and `eps`.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not write to co_bus.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None; ActionHead logs masks if debug enabled.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Indirect via `qa.sh` mask semantics.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/08_TRANSLATORS/maze_translator.md <<'EOF'\n# Maze Translator\n\n## Purpose\nScore maze moves based on goal distance, density, and visit penalty; emit blocklist mask for walls.\n\n## Inputs\n- Observation: `pos`, `goal`, `grid`, `width`, `height`\n- Signals: `EG_DensityPrecision.visit_density`, `EA_HAQ.novelty`\n\n## Outputs\n- `(scores: Dict[str,float], translator_mask: set, info: dict)`\n- `translator_mask` contains blocked moves (walls/out of bounds).\n\n## State mutation\n- None.\n\n## Algorithm\n- Score moves by Manhattan improvement, minus density/visited penalties, plus novelty.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not change environment.\n\n## Telemetry\n- Mask semantics verified by QA if mask fields are present.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `qa.sh` mask semantics check should pass on maze smoke run.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/08_TRANSLATORS/renewal_translator.md <<'EOF'\n# Renewal Translator\n\n## Purpose\nScore renewal symbols using n-gram model or predict-last fallback.\n\n## Inputs\n- Observation: `A`, `obs`\n- Primitive: `ngram_model`\n\n## Outputs\n- `(scores: Dict[int,float], translator_mask: set, info: dict)`\n- Mask is usually empty for renewal.\n\n## State mutation\n- None.\n\n## Algorithm\n- If n-gram model available, use `predict_proba`, else predict last observation.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not mutate primitives.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None directly.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not part of QA smoke path by default.\n\nEOF\n\n# ---- ACCEPTANCE ----\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/09_ACCEPTANCE/QA_GATES.md <<'EOF'\n# QA Gates\n\n## Mandatory Gate\n- `ChangeOntCode/tools/qa.sh` must pass before merge.\n\n## What QA Checks\n- Header record existence\n- Header update source (when present)\n- Required signals keys\n- Identity variation and last_d positive\n- GHVC birth suggest + birth_count change\n- Mask semantics\n- Exactly one co_debug per t\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/09_ACCEPTANCE/SMOKE_CONFIGS.md <<'EOF'\n# Smoke Configs\n\n## QA Smoke Configs (fast)\n- `outputs/verify/configs/qa_bandit.yaml`\n- `outputs/verify/configs/qa_maze.yaml`\n\n## QA-Only Agent Variant\n- `CO_full_QA` lives in `experiments/configs/co_agents/co_agents_selection.yaml` and is for QA evidence only.\n- `CO_full` remains the real/default CO variant.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/09_ACCEPTANCE/SPEC_GAPS.md <<'EOF'\n# Spec Gaps (Future Work)\n\nThese items are referenced in legacy annex docs but are not present in code:\n- `core/headers/collapse.py`\n- `core/headers/meta_flip.py`\n- `core/quotient/equivalence.py`\n- `core/quotient/infimum_lift.py`\n- `evaluation/invariance_test.py`\n- `tests/test_lift.py`\n- `tests/test_logic.py`\n\nThese are **FUTURE** and not required for current kernel acceptance or QA.\n\nEOF\n","yield_time_ms":1000} thread_id=019c9b92-4551-7730-a36c-a30f295a6bf4
