2026-02-26T22:56:11.932779Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019c9b92-4551-7730-a36c-a30f295a6bf4}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec_command {"cmd":"cat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/04_PRIMITIVES/P1_BendMetric.md <<'EOF'\n# P1_BendMetric\n\n## Purpose\nCompute bend distance between traces for identity decisions.\n\n## Inputs (exact keys/types; where read from)\n- `trace`: list of action tokens (strings or ints). Source: `observation[\"history\"]` or `observation[\"trace\"]`.\n- `eps`: float threshold from header state (read by EC_Identity).\n\n## Outputs (exact vote families, signals keys, return dict fields)\n- Returns a non-negative float distance `D(trace_a, trace_b)`.\n\n## State mutation (what is allowed to change; where state is stored)\n- None. P1 is pure and must not mutate shared state.\n\n## Algorithm (step-by-step; include constants/thresholds if binding)\n**Trace representation v1**\n- A trace is an ordered list of tokens. Tokens are compared by equality.\n- If `trace` is missing or empty, treat it as an empty list.\n\n**Distance v1 (warped-Hamming with PAD cost)**\n1. Let `A` and `B` be two traces.\n2. Let `L = max(len(A), len(B))`.\n3. Define PAD token `__PAD__`.\n4. Pad the shorter trace to length `L` with PAD.\n5. Distance is the count of positions where tokens differ:\n   - `D(A,B) = sum(1 for i in 0..L-1 if A[i] != B[i])`.\n\n**Downstream use**\n- Identity decision uses `identity_ok = (last_d <= eps)`.\n\n## Forbidden (explicit anti-smuggling rules)\n- Must not read hidden environment state.\n- Must not mutate any shared or global state.\n\n## Telemetry (exact metrics.jsonl / co_debug fields and signals dict keys)\n- `signals[\"EC_Identity.same\"]` and `signals[\"EC_Identity.last_d\"]` are emitted by EC_Identity using this distance.\n\n## Acceptance (exact reviewer procedure: which smoke run, which qa.sh checks, what evidence line(s) prove it)\n- Run `outputs/verify/configs/qa_bandit.yaml` and `outputs/verify/configs/qa_maze.yaml`.\n- `qa.sh` must pass `signals_present` and `identity_variation`.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/04_PRIMITIVES/P10_ChangeOpsCore.md <<'EOF'\n# P10_ChangeOpsCore\n\n## Purpose\nMaintain the canonical prototype store used by GHVC births.\n\n## Inputs\n- Birth acceptance signal from EB_GHVC.\n- Optional history/trace from observation for prototype construction.\n\n## Outputs\n- Prototype list used to compute `prototype_count` and equivalence classes.\n\n## State mutation\n- **Canonical location:** `primitives[\"P10\"]`.\n- **Canonical structure:** `primitives[\"P10\"].prototypes` is a list.\n- EB_GHVC appends a new prototype when birth is accepted.\n\n## Algorithm\n1. If birth is accepted and `primitives[\"P10\"]` is missing, instantiate `ChangeOpsCore` and store it at `primitives[\"P10\"]`.\n2. If `history`/`trace` is available, append the last `k` tokens as a tuple; otherwise append a unique token like `(family, t)`.\n\n## Forbidden\n- No alternative stores for prototypes (`primitives[\"p10\"]`, `primitives[\"change_ops\"]`, etc.) are allowed.\n- Must not overwrite existing prototypes list; only append new entries.\n\n## Telemetry\n- EB_GHVC emits `prototype_count`, `merge_events`, `split_events`, and `birth_count` derived from this state.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `qa.sh` must pass `ghvc_birth` on QA smoke configs.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/04_PRIMITIVES/P12_ClosureQuotient.md <<'EOF'\n# P12_ClosureQuotient\n\n## Purpose\nCompute minimal equivalence closure over prototypes using bend distance.\n\n## Inputs\n- Prototype list from `primitives[\"P10\"].prototypes`.\n- Bend distance function from P1.\n- Epsilon threshold from header (if stored in P12 instance).\n\n## Outputs\n- List of classes (each class is a list of prototypes).\n- `class_count = len(classes)`.\n\n## State mutation\n- None required; P12 may store epsilon locally.\n\n## Algorithm (Minimal Closure v1)\n1. Initialize each prototype as its own class.\n2. Merge classes if any pair across classes has `bend_distance <= eps`.\n3. Repeat until no merges remain.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Do not implement advanced quotient/equivalence/infimum-lift here. Those belong in SPEC_GAPS.\n\n## Telemetry\n- EB_GHVC emits `class_count` based on closure results.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Indirectly verified through `qa.sh` `ghvc_birth` and `signals_present`.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/05_ELEMENTS/EB_GHVC.md <<'EOF'\n# EB_GHVC\n\n## Purpose\nBirth suggestion and variable creation based on residual/probe signals.\n\n## Inputs (exact keys/types; where read from)\n- `observation.residuals` (dict, optional)\n- `observation.probes` (dict, optional)\n- `observation.feedback` or `feedback` (dict, optional; uses `reward`)\n- `header` (for epsilon context)\n- `primitives[\"budget\"]` (optional)\n\n## Outputs (exact vote families, signals keys, return dict fields)\n- Signals (scalar store):\n  - `signals[\"EB_GHVC.pressure\"]`\n  - `signals[\"EB_GHVC.mdl_gain\"]`\n  - `signals[\"EB_GHVC.birth_suggest\"]`\n- Counters:\n  - `birth_events`, `merge_events`, `split_events`, `prototype_count`, `class_count`, `cap_hits`, `birth_count`\n\n## State mutation (what is allowed to change; where state is stored)\n- May create/update `primitives[\"P10\"]` and `primitives[\"P12\"]`.\n- Updates `primitives[\"birth_count\"]` (monotonic counter).\n\n## Algorithm (step-by-step; include constants/thresholds if binding)\n**Parameters (binding names)**\n- `gamma` comes from element params `gamma` or `birth_threshold`.\n- `lam_mdl` comes from element params `lambda` or `mdl_lambda`.\n\n**Pressure computation v1**\n1. Read `mse = residuals.mse` (float) and `cp = probes.change_point` (float), default 0.\n2. If both are 0 and `feedback.reward` exists, set `mse = abs(reward) * 4.5`.\n3. `pressure = 0.5 * mse + 0.5 * cp`.\n\n**MDL gain v1**\n- `k_new = 0` if residuals and probes are empty; else `k_new = 1`.\n- `mdl_gain = max(0, mse) - lam_mdl * k_new`.\n\n**Birth accept v1**\n- `born_variable = (pressure > gamma) and (mdl_gain > 0)`.\n- If budget exists, require `budget.allow_move(\"birth\")` and `budget.commit(\"birth\")`.\n\n**Mutation v1**\n- If birth accepted: append a prototype into `primitives[\"P10\"].prototypes` (see P10 spec).\n- Recompute `prototype_count` and `class_count` using P12 closure.\n- Update `birth_count += 1`.\n\n## Forbidden (explicit anti-smuggling rules)\n- Must not emit votes to `co_bus` (signals only).\n- Must not mutate header state.\n\n## Telemetry (exact metrics.jsonl / co_debug fields and signals dict keys)\n- Required signals: `EB_GHVC.pressure`, `EB_GHVC.mdl_gain`, `EB_GHVC.birth_suggest`.\n- Required counters when present: `birth_count`, `birth_events`, `prototype_count`.\n\n## Acceptance (exact reviewer procedure: which smoke run, which qa.sh checks, what evidence line(s) prove it)\n- Run `outputs/verify/configs/qa_bandit.yaml` or `qa_maze.yaml`.\n- `qa.sh` must pass `signals_present` and `ghvc_birth`.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/06_HEADERS/H_SSI.md <<'EOF'\n# H_SSI\n\n## Purpose\nSelf-situated inference header (default for CO).\n\n## Inputs\n- Observation envelope in `run_update` (may include `feedback`).\n\n## Outputs\n- Header state fields used by ActionHead (e.g., `co_weight` if present).\n\n## State mutation\n- Header state may mutate **only** in `run_update`.\n\n## Binding Contract (v1)\n- Header must expose a `.state` object/dict.\n- ActionHead may read `header.state.co_weight` (default 1.0 if absent).\n- Header must not be updated in decision pass.\n\n## Forbidden\n- No decision-pass mutation.\n- No direct writes to `co_bus`.\n\n## Telemetry\n- `debug_header_updates` is allowed when `CO_DEBUG_HEADER=1`.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `qa.sh` must pass `header_update_source` when present.\n\n## Non-binding / Future\n- Exact SSI equations are **not** specified here; if needed, add to `09_ACCEPTANCE/SPEC_GAPS.md` and implement in header code.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/06_HEADERS/H_CS.md <<'EOF'\n# H_CS\n\n## Purpose\nClassical-slice header (CO off).\n\n## Inputs\n- Observation envelope in `run_update`.\n\n## Outputs\n- Header state fields indicating classical-only operation.\n\n## State mutation\n- Update only in `run_update`.\n\n## Binding Contract (v1)\n- Must provide `.state` for ActionHead reads (even if empty).\n- Must not be updated in decision pass.\n\n## Forbidden\n- No decision-pass mutation.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None required.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not gated by QA unless configured.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/06_HEADERS/H_ID.md <<'EOF'\n# H_ID\n\n## Purpose\nIdentity-first header (fixed epsilon policy).\n\n## Inputs\n- Observation envelope in `run_update`.\n\n## Outputs\n- Header state fields for identity policy.\n\n## State mutation\n- Update only in `run_update`.\n\n## Binding Contract (v1)\n- Must provide `.state` for ActionHead reads.\n- Must not be updated in decision pass.\n\n## Forbidden\n- No decision-pass mutation.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None required.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Not gated by QA unless configured.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/07_COMBINATORS/C_Gate.md <<'EOF'\n# C_Gate\n\n## Purpose\nNot used in v1 canonical runtime.\n\n## Inputs\n- N/A (not used).\n\n## Outputs\n- N/A (not used).\n\n## State mutation\n- None.\n\n## Algorithm\n- Do not implement for v1.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not introduce alternate runtime paths.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None.\n\n## Acceptance\n- N/A (future only).\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/05_ELEMENTS/EF_Router.md <<'EOF'\n# EF_Router\n\n## Purpose\nNot used in v1 canonical runtime.\n\n## Inputs\n- N/A (not used).\n\n## Outputs\n- N/A (not used).\n\n## State mutation\n- None.\n\n## Algorithm\n- Do not implement for v1.\n\n## Forbidden\n- Must not introduce alternate runtime paths.\n\n## Telemetry\n- None.\n\n## Acceptance\n- N/A (future only).\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/09_ACCEPTANCE/SPEC_GAPS.md <<'EOF'\n# Spec Gaps (Future Work)\n\nThese items are referenced in legacy annex docs but are not present in code:\n- `core/headers/collapse.py`\n- `core/headers/meta_flip.py`\n- `core/quotient/equivalence.py`\n- `core/quotient/infimum_lift.py`\n- `evaluation/invariance_test.py`\n- `tests/test_lift.py`\n- `tests/test_logic.py`\n\nAdditional future work:\n- Advanced quotient/equivalence logic beyond P12 minimal closure v1\n- Concrete SSI/H_ID/H_CS equations if needed for formal proofs\n- C_Gate and EF_Router behavior (not used in v1)\n\nThese are **FUTURE** and not required for current kernel acceptance or QA.\n\nEOF\n\ncat > ChangeOntCode/docs/kernel_spec/03_WIRING_MAP.md <<'EOF'\n# Wiring Map\n\n## Elements -> Primitives -> Signals (Current Implementation)\n- `EA_HAQ` -> publishes `EA_HAQ.novelty` (if present)\n- `EB_GHVC` -> uses `P10` and `P12`, publishes:\n  - `EB_GHVC.pressure`, `EB_GHVC.mdl_gain`, `EB_GHVC.birth_suggest`\n  - `birth_events`, `merge_events`, `split_events`, `prototype_count`, `class_count`, `cap_hits`, `birth_count`\n- `EC_Identity` -> uses P1 bend metric and trace memory, publishes:\n  - `EC_Identity.same`, `EC_Identity.last_d`, `bend_triggers`\n- `EG_DensityPrecision` -> publishes `EG_DensityPrecision.visit_density` (if present)\n- `VoteBridge` -> publishes votes via `co_bus.push(...)`\n- `ActionHead` -> drains votes, applies translator mask, emits `signals` snapshot and derived convenience fields\n\n## Implemented vs Future\n- Implemented: `EA_HAQ`, `EB_GHVC`, `EC_Identity`, `EG_DensityPrecision`, `VoteBridge`, `ActionHead`\n- Future (see `09_ACCEPTANCE/SPEC_GAPS.md`): advanced quotient/equivalence/infimum-lift, meta_flip, collapse, invariance tests, C_Gate, EF_Router\n\nEOF\n","yield_time_ms":1000,"max_output_tokens":2000} thread_id=019c9b92-4551-7730-a36c-a30f295a6bf4
